  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize forming three pure sets (tunnelas or pure sequences) so you can choose or see the tiplu. Avoid discarding cards that complete opponents' sets.\n\nTrack which cards have been discarded and estimate the tiplu from the first player who lays down. Use the three-deck composition to plan trials and sequences.\n\nBalance going out quickly versus collecting maal (tiplu, poplu, jhiplu) for points. A marriage (one jhiplu, one tiplu, one poplu) scores 10 points.",
